795 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 609 0 R
/T (Sanctions relief constitutes a necessary settlement component. Oil and gas revenues fell below 23 percent of Russia's federal budget in 2025, yet fiscal pressure continues to compound: the Bank of Russia cut its key rate six consecutive times to 15.5 percent from a 21 percent peak, GDP growth decelerated from 4.1 percent in 2024 to approximately 1 percent in 2025, and KSE Institute projects oil export revenues at $106 billion in 2026, down from $189 billion in 2024.6 The draft peace plan proposes sanctions removal "in stages and on a case-by-case basis" with snapback provisions, a marked retreat from Moscow's demand for immediate unconditional removal. The JCPOA precedent and the Atlantic Council's eleven guiding principles, with benchmarks tied to child returns, POW releases, and withdrawal milestones, provide actionable frameworks for phased relief.7)
/E (Sanctions relief constitutes a necessary settlement component. Oil and gas revenues fell below 23 percent of Russia's federal budget in 2025, yet fiscal pressure continues to compound: the Bank of Russia cut its key rate six consecutive times to 15.5 percent from a 21 percent peak, GDP growth decelerated from 4.1 percent in 2024 to approximately 1 percent in 2025, and KSE Institute projects oil export revenues at $106 billion in 2026, down from $189 billion in 2024.6 The draft peace plan proposes sanctions removal "in stages and on a case-by-case basis" with snapback provisions, a marked retreat from Moscow's demand for immediate unconditional removal. The JCPOA precedent and the Atlantic Council's eleven guiding principles, with benchmarks tied to child returns, POW releases, and withdrawal milestones, provide actionable frameworks for phased relief.7)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [31 33 32 34]
>>
endobj
796 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 609 0 R
/T (The optimal approach follows a three-phase sequence: tighten enforcement to close the revenue-denial gap and establish credibility \(Phase I\), hold at maximum demonstrated pressure during initial negotiations \(Phase II\), and offer calibrated relief, graduated by value, reversibility, and compliance milestone, with preserved snapback authority \(Phase III\). Relief tiers should range from low-value, high-reversibility measures, such as vessel delistings at ceasefire implementation, to high-value concessions such as partial SWIFT reconnection that require verified comprehensive settlement compliance. )
/E (The optimal approach follows a three-phase sequence: tighten enforcement to close the revenue-denial gap and establish credibility \(Phase I\), hold at maximum demonstrated pressure during initial negotiations \(Phase II\), and offer calibrated relief, graduated by value, reversibility, and compliance milestone, with preserved snapback authority \(Phase III\). Relief tiers should range from low-value, high-reversibility measures, such as vessel delistings at ceasefire implementation, to high-value concessions such as partial SWIFT reconnection that require verified comprehensive settlement compliance. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [35]
>>
endobj
797 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 609 0 R
/T (Coalition unity is the critical constraint: the United States controls OFAC designations and secondary sanctions authority while the EU controls the dynamic cap and SWIFT reconnection, and explicit instrument-assignment between Washington and Brussels is the essential precondition.8 The appropriate success metric is not sanctions volume, but the degree to which calibrated pressure and credible relief produce verifiable behavioral change toward a durable settlement.)
/E (Coalition unity is the critical constraint: the United States controls OFAC designations and secondary sanctions authority while the EU controls the dynamic cap and SWIFT reconnection, and explicit instrument-assignment between Washington and Brussels is the essential precondition.8 The appropriate success metric is not sanctions volume, but the degree to which calibrated pressure and credible relief produce verifiable behavioral change toward a durable settlement.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [36 38 37]
>>
