/T (The decisive U.S.-controlled variable is secondary sanctions authority over India and China, which together absorb roughly 85 percent of Russian seaborne crude.14 The recommended approach follows a three-phase sequence: tighten enforcement to close the revenue-denial gap and establish credibility, hold at maximum demonstrated pressure during initial negotiations, then offer calibrated relief, graduated by value, reversibility, and compliance milestone, with preserved snapback authority.)
