/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 612 0 R
/T (The cap operates not as a direct ceiling on Russian oil sales but as a prohibition that bars Western service providers, shippers, insurers, brokers, and trade financiers, from service to Russian crude shipments sold above the cap. Enforcement depends on a three-tier attestation system in which brokers retain price records, financial institutions and shipping agents obtain attestations, and insurers verify compliance per voyage.17 The structural weakness: P&I clubs that insure the vast majority of global commercial shipping have no independent price verification capability and depend entirely on upstream self-attestation. The International Group of P&I Clubs acknowledged this fundamental reliance on attestation integrity.18 By mid-2023, Bruegel found that 96 percent of Russian crude exports from Kozmino port carried prices above the cap; attestation fraud was systemic from the regime's earliest months.19 OFAC tightened the framework in December 2023 through per-voyage attestation requirements and itemized cost documentation mandates, but these patches addressed symptoms and failed to resolve the structural self-attestation dependency.20 The distance between the cap's theoretical coverage and actual compliance defines the enforcement gap quantified below.)
/E (The cap operates not as a direct ceiling on Russian oil sales but as a prohibition that bars Western service providers, shippers, insurers, brokers, and trade financiers, from service to Russian crude shipments sold above the cap. Enforcement depends on a three-tier attestation system in which brokers retain price records, financial institutions and shipping agents obtain attestations, and insurers verify compliance per voyage.17 The structural weakness: P&I clubs that insure the vast majority of global commercial shipping have no independent price verification capability and depend entirely on upstream self-attestation. The International Group of P&I Clubs acknowledged this fundamental reliance on attestation integrity.18 By mid-2023, Bruegel found that 96 percent of Russian crude exports from Kozmino port carried prices above the cap; attestation fraud was systemic from the regime's earliest months.19 OFAC tightened the framework in December 2023 through per-voyage attestation requirements and itemized cost documentation mandates, but these patches addressed symptoms and failed to resolve the structural self-attestation dependency.20 The distance between the cap's theoretical coverage and actual compliance defines the enforcement gap quantified below.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [16 21 17 22 18 23 19 24 20]
