/T (Hungary's veto threat forced an exemption for pipeline crude through the Druzhba system, which continued to supply Hungary, Slovakia, and the Czech Republic at an estimated 5-6 billion euros annually in Russian revenues.22 The Czech Republic eliminated its dependence by April 2025 via the TAL-PLUS alternative; Slovakia remains reliant. Petroleum product caps \($100/barrel premium, $45/barrel discount\) remain static; the floating mechanism applies only to crude.)
