919 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 615 0 R
/T (Russian fossil fuel export revenues declined 54 percent from their post-invasion peak, from approximately 1,000 million euros per day in March 2022 to 464 million euros per day in January 2026, the lowest level since the full-scale invasion.32 The decline occurred in four distinct phases. The first \(February-November 2022\) produced a counterintuitive surge as commodity price spikes pushed revenues to approximately 868 million euros per day, and Russia earned 158 billion euros before the cap took effect. The second \(December 2022-mid-2023\) captured the cap's initial impact: revenues dropped to 640-700 million euros per day then stabilized as the shadow fleet scaled and attestation fraud spread. The third \(mid-2023-mid-2025\) traced a sustained but slow decline through the 600s, with the January 2025 OFAC designations an accelerant.)
/E (Russian fossil fuel export revenues declined 54 percent from their post-invasion peak, from approximately 1,000 million euros per day in March 2022 to 464 million euros per day in January 2026, the lowest level since the full-scale invasion.32 The decline occurred in four distinct phases. The first \(February-November 2022\) produced a counterintuitive surge as commodity price spikes pushed revenues to approximately 868 million euros per day, and Russia earned 158 billion euros before the cap took effect. The second \(December 2022-mid-2023\) captured the cap's initial impact: revenues dropped to 640-700 million euros per day then stabilized as the shadow fleet scaled and attestation fraud spread. The third \(mid-2023-mid-2025\) traced a sustained but slow decline through the 600s, with the January 2025 OFAC designations an accelerant.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [21 23 22]
