/T (The fourth phase \(September 2025-January 2026\) produced the sharpest compression and carries direct implications for the leverage assessment. The floating cap, Rosneft and Lukoil designations, and secondary sanctions effects combined to drive revenues from 546 million euros per day in September to 464 in January, a four-month decline that exceeded the previous year's total erosion. The IEA's February 2026 Oil Market Report independently characterized Russian oil revenues as "roughly half pre-invasion levels."33)
