/T (KSE Institute's forward projections quantify the enforcement gap's fiscal trajectory. The December 2025 Oil Tracker revised the 2026 oil export revenue projection to $106 billion, a $25 billion downward revision from October's $131 billion estimate in a single month; under strong enforcement, KSE projects 2026 revenues as low as $67 billion.43  The fiscal impact at the sharp end is already visible: January 2026 oil and gas tax revenue fell 50 percent year-on-year to 393 billion rubles, 232 billion below the budget plan, which assumed $59 per barrel Urals, now far above market reality.44)
