/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 620 0 R
/T (The quantitative evidence supports a calibrated assessment: the sanctions architecture works but operates well below its design potential. The Bank of Finland, among the most authoritative independent monitors of the Russian economy, published a January 2026 analysis with a section titled "Sanctions have worked": Urals-Brent discounts widened from $1-2 to over $20; the National Wealth Fund's liquid assets depleted; GDP growth constrained to approximately 1 percent; Gazprom posted net losses of $7 billion \(2023\) and $12.89 billion \(2024\).45 The GAO, through synthetic control methodology, found Russia's 2022 growth was approximately 6 percentage points below a no-sanctions counterfactual.46 CSIS characterized the Russian economy as "down but not out" and the sanctions toolkit as "among the most potent weapons to contain Russian power."47)
/E (The quantitative evidence supports a calibrated assessment: the sanctions architecture works but operates well below its design potential. The Bank of Finland, among the most authoritative independent monitors of the Russian economy, published a January 2026 analysis with a section titled "Sanctions have worked": Urals-Brent discounts widened from $1-2 to over $20; the National Wealth Fund's liquid assets depleted; GDP growth constrained to approximately 1 percent; Gazprom posted net losses of $7 billion \(2023\) and $12.89 billion \(2024\).45 The GAO, through synthetic control methodology, found Russia's 2022 growth was approximately 6 percentage points below a no-sanctions counterfactual.46 CSIS characterized the Russian economy as "down but not out" and the sanctions toolkit as "among the most potent weapons to contain Russian power."47)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [26 29 27 30 28 31]
>>
endobj
1021 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 620 0 R
/T (The underperformance evidence is equally documented. CREA's counterfactual analyses consistently identify substantial additional denial achievable under tighter enforcement, from 13-17 percent under the current cap to the 162 billion euro gap under a $30 threshold. The FREE Network found that by early 2025, only 15 percent of crude tankers that departed Russian ports used Western insurance.48 The analytical framework that connects these findings comes from Brookings and Harvard. Brooks, Harris, and Marshall \(June 2025\) argued that "Russia is more exposed to Western sanctions than it was at the start of its invasion" and that Western nations possess "generally more leverage."49 Craig Kennedy \(Harvard Davis Center, May 2025\) framed the enforcement gap explicitly as a policy asset: shadow fleet capacity fell 46 percent after Q1 2025 sanctions, and "Moscow's rising dependency on mainstream tankers provides policymakers with enhanced leverage."50 Brooks and Harris characterized the price cap and vessel sanctions as "a graduated escalation ladder," adjustable, reversible, and under policymaker control.51)
/E (The underperformance evidence is equally documented. CREA's counterfactual analyses consistently identify substantial additional denial achievable under tighter enforcement, from 13-17 percent under the current cap to the 162 billion euro gap under a $30 threshold. The FREE Network found that by early 2025, only 15 percent of crude tankers that departed Russian ports used Western insurance.48 The analytical framework that connects these findings comes from Brookings and Harvard. Brooks, Harris, and Marshall \(June 2025\) argued that "Russia is more exposed to Western sanctions than it was at the start of its invasion" and that Western nations possess "generally more leverage."49 Craig Kennedy \(Harvard Davis Center, May 2025\) framed the enforcement gap explicitly as a policy asset: shadow fleet capacity fell 46 percent after Q1 2025 sanctions, and "Moscow's rising dependency on mainstream tankers provides policymakers with enhanced leverage."50 Brooks and Harris characterized the price cap and vessel sanctions as "a graduated escalation ladder," adjustable, reversible, and under policymaker control.51)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [32 36 33 37 34 38 35 39]
>>
