/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 629 0 R
/T (The United States controls the architecture's most potent coercive instruments through OFAC: SDN designations with the unique productivity differential the preceding subsection documented, secondary sanctions authority under Executive Order 14024 \(no EU equivalent exists\), and granular calibration through general licenses.82 The EU controls three of Russia's highest-priority relief targets: SWIFT access \(governed by Belgian law\), frozen Central Bank reserves of approximately 200 billion euros held primarily at Euroclear, and the floating cap and its proposed maritime ban successor.83 The United Kingdom holds a distinctive position through London's insurance infrastructure, with the International Group of P&I Clubs' coverage of 86 to 95 percent of the global commercial fleet.84 EU sanctions require unanimity under Article 29 TEU, which means any single member state can block both escalation and relief.)
/E (The United States controls the architecture's most potent coercive instruments through OFAC: SDN designations with the unique productivity differential the preceding subsection documented, secondary sanctions authority under Executive Order 14024 \(no EU equivalent exists\), and granular calibration through general licenses.82 The EU controls three of Russia's highest-priority relief targets: SWIFT access \(governed by Belgian law\), frozen Central Bank reserves of approximately 200 billion euros held primarily at Euroclear, and the floating cap and its proposed maritime ban successor.83 The United Kingdom holds a distinctive position through London's insurance infrastructure, with the International Group of P&I Clubs' coverage of 86 to 95 percent of the global commercial fleet.84 EU sanctions require unanimity under Article 29 TEU, which means any single member state can block both escalation and relief.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [24 28 25 29 26 30 27]
