1205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 629 0 R
/T (Russia's position on sanctions relief evolved from maximalist rejection to operational flexibility. The peace draft under discussion proposes removal "in stages and on a case-by-case basis, with snapback provisions," which CEPA characterizes as "a significant Russian retreat from its long-held position that all sanctions are illegal and must be removed immediately."85 Russia's revealed instrument priorities confirm the stakes: SWIFT reconnection ranks as the top operational demand and falls under EU control; correspondent banking and oil export restrictions follow; and Russia appears to have accepted de facto that the frozen reserves are unlikely to return, with the Central Bank's December 2025 legal proceedings against Euroclear consistent with write-off rather than recovery.86)
/E (Russia's position on sanctions relief evolved from maximalist rejection to operational flexibility. The peace draft under discussion proposes removal "in stages and on a case-by-case basis, with snapback provisions," which CEPA characterizes as "a significant Russian retreat from its long-held position that all sanctions are illegal and must be removed immediately."85 Russia's revealed instrument priorities confirm the stakes: SWIFT reconnection ranks as the top operational demand and falls under EU control; correspondent banking and oil export restrictions follow; and Russia appears to have accepted de facto that the frozen reserves are unlikely to return, with the Central Bank's December 2025 legal proceedings against Euroclear consistent with write-off rather than recovery.86)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [32 34 33 35]
>>
endobj
1206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 629 0 R
/T (The JCPOA offers the closest precedent for staged, verification-triggered multilateral sanctions relief. Implementation Day on January 16, 2016, demonstrated that simultaneous multi-actor relief tied to independent verification is technically achievable: the IAEA verified Iran's completion of fifteen nuclear-related actions, and the EU, United States, and United Nations lifted sanctions in coordinated sequence.87 The 2018 U.S. withdrawal, however, destroyed the framework without activating its own enforcement architecture, and Iran began to exceed nuclear limits by July 2019; Moscow explicitly cites this precedent, with Lavrov calling the snapback mechanism "a trap."88 The "JCPOA chill" reinforced the lesson from the economic side: despite formal relief, few Western firms returned to Iran, as residual sanctions, banking de-risking, and snapback risk combined to limit tangible economic benefit.89)
/E (The JCPOA offers the closest precedent for staged, verification-triggered multilateral sanctions relief. Implementation Day on January 16, 2016, demonstrated that simultaneous multi-actor relief tied to independent verification is technically achievable: the IAEA verified Iran's completion of fifteen nuclear-related actions, and the EU, United States, and United Nations lifted sanctions in coordinated sequence.87 The 2018 U.S. withdrawal, however, destroyed the framework without activating its own enforcement architecture, and Iran began to exceed nuclear limits by July 2019; Moscow explicitly cites this precedent, with Lavrov calling the snapback mechanism "a trap."88 The "JCPOA chill" reinforced the lesson from the economic side: despite formal relief, few Western firms returned to Iran, as residual sanctions, banking de-risking, and snapback risk combined to limit tangible economic benefit.89)
