/T (The empirical record through early 2026 establishes a fundamental asymmetry: any coalition member can tighten unilaterally, but meaningful relief requires joint action. Throughout 2025, the EU and UK adopted major sanctions packages without U.S. participation, the EU lowered the cap unilaterally, and the UK designated entities the EU had not matched.94 he relief side inverts this logic. Russia requires OFAC designation removal \(U.S.-controlled\), SWIFT reconnection \(EU-controlled\), frozen asset access \(EU-controlled\), insurance market reopening \(UK-controlled\), and cap removal \(joint\). )
/E (The empirical record through early 2026 establishes a fundamental asymmetry: any coalition member can tighten unilaterally, but meaningful relief requires joint action. Throughout 2025, the EU and UK adopted major sanctions packages without U.S. participation, the EU lowered the cap unilaterally, and the UK designated entities the EU had not matched.94 he relief side inverts this logic. Russia requires OFAC designation removal \(U.S.-controlled\), SWIFT reconnection \(EU-controlled\), frozen asset access \(EU-controlled\), insurance market reopening \(UK-controlled\), and cap removal \(joint\). )
