/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 634 0 R
/T (The first action targets the vessel designation gap. OFAC has not designated a single Russia-specific vessel since January 2025, even as the EU has added vessels in monthly rolling actions. Against the estimated 940-vessel shadow fleet and approximately 700-800 unique designations across jurisdictions, the gap stands at approximately 140-240 vessels.105 The Envoy's Office should coordinate an OFAC designation package with priority on tankers that transit Baltic chokepoints, which carry 60 percent of Russian seaborne crude exports, and those that conduct ship-to-ship transfers at identified hotspots. The fourteen-nation stateless vessel declaration of January 2026 creates complementary enforcement under UNCLOS Article 110: over 300 shadow fleet vessels fly false or no flags, which subjects them to interdiction by signatory navies.)
/E (The first action targets the vessel designation gap. OFAC has not designated a single Russia-specific vessel since January 2025, even as the EU has added vessels in monthly rolling actions. Against the estimated 940-vessel shadow fleet and approximately 700-800 unique designations across jurisdictions, the gap stands at approximately 140-240 vessels.105 The Envoy's Office should coordinate an OFAC designation package with priority on tankers that transit Baltic chokepoints, which carry 60 percent of Russian seaborne crude exports, and those that conduct ship-to-ship transfers at identified hotspots. The fourteen-nation stateless vessel declaration of January 2026 creates complementary enforcement under UNCLOS Article 110: over 300 shadow fleet vessels fly false or no flags, which subjects them to interdiction by signatory navies.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [21 23 22]
>>
endobj
1296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 634 0 R
/T (The second action formalizes Nordic and Baltic enforcement coordination. Denmark, Sweden, and Germany now require insurance documentation from transit tankers, with over 90 percent of contacted vessels eventually in compliance. The NB8++ insurance verification initiative and the JEF-led Nordic Warden AI system provide real-time shadow fleet surveillance across twelve countries.106 Phase I should convert this ad hoc coordination into a standing Baltic enforcement mechanism. The environmental liability argument provides the strategic rationale: the shadow fleet's average age of 18-19 years creates acute spill risk in confined Baltic waters, and environmental framing expands the enforcement coalition beyond sanctions-focused actors.)
/E (The second action formalizes Nordic and Baltic enforcement coordination. Denmark, Sweden, and Germany now require insurance documentation from transit tankers, with over 90 percent of contacted vessels eventually in compliance. The NB8++ insurance verification initiative and the JEF-led Nordic Warden AI system provide real-time shadow fleet surveillance across twelve countries.106 Phase I should convert this ad hoc coordination into a standing Baltic enforcement mechanism. The environmental liability argument provides the strategic rationale: the shadow fleet's average age of 18-19 years creates acute spill risk in confined Baltic waters, and environmental framing expands the enforcement coalition beyond sanctions-focused actors.)
