/T (Phase II should establish a public enforcement dashboard that reports monthly revenue denial figures, vessel compliance rates, price spread data, and volume shifts. No government currently publishes systematic sanctions effectiveness data; CREA and KSE already provide the analytical architecture, and an official U.S. version would carry additional institutional weight. The dashboard serves three audiences: Moscow, by demonstration that the regime's coercive capacity is measured and publicized; coalition partners, by sustained domestic political support; and Congress, by construction of the evidentiary case for eventual Phase III relief authority.)
