/S /H1
/P 637 0 R
/T (The snapback architecture must address Moscow's explicit skepticism about U.S. commitment durability; Lavrov characterized the JCPOA snapback as "a trap."114 The FDD's general license approach provides the most operationally sound mechanism: entities remain on the SDN list throughout all three phases, and relief comes exclusively through revocable licenses. Formal SDN delisting, which requires 12-18 months for re-designation, should occur only at the final stage of comprehensive settlement compliance, years into the process. Russia's UNSC veto makes Council-based snapback architecture impossible; any mechanism must therefore operate on a purely plurilateral basis among G7 and coalition partners. CAATSA-covered designations face 30-day congressional review even for relief, a deliberate institutional brake that the Envoy should treat as a credibility asset rather than a constraint.115)
/E (The snapback architecture must address Moscow's explicit skepticism about U.S. commitment durability; Lavrov characterized the JCPOA snapback as "a trap."114 The FDD's general license approach provides the most operationally sound mechanism: entities remain on the SDN list throughout all three phases, and relief comes exclusively through revocable licenses. Formal SDN delisting, which requires 12-18 months for re-designation, should occur only at the final stage of comprehensive settlement compliance, years into the process. Russia's UNSC veto makes Council-based snapback architecture impossible; any mechanism must therefore operate on a purely plurilateral basis among G7 and coalition partners. CAATSA-covered designations face 30-day congressional review even for relief, a deliberate institutional brake that the Envoy should treat as a credibility asset rather than a constraint.115)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [16 18 17 19]
>>
endobj
1344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 637 0 R
/T (Verification requires a hybrid architecture that bypasses the OSCE consensus problem, since Russia vetoed mandate renewal in March 2022. The alternative combines commercial satellite and AIS surveillance \(Windward, Maxar/Planet/ICEYE\), the U.S.-involved monitoring mechanism under discussion at the Geneva and Abu Dhabi rounds, and open-source intelligence from established platforms \(KSE Oil Tracker, CREA monthly analyses, Kpler vessel data\).116 A dedicated commercial satellite verification program would cost an estimated $5 to $50 million annually, a fraction of the OSCE SMM's peak budget of over 100 million euros and orders of magnitude less than the revenue at stake.)
/E (Verification requires a hybrid architecture that bypasses the OSCE consensus problem, since Russia vetoed mandate renewal in March 2022. The alternative combines commercial satellite and AIS surveillance \(Windward, Maxar/Planet/ICEYE\), the U.S.-involved monitoring mechanism under discussion at the Geneva and Abu Dhabi rounds, and open-source intelligence from established platforms \(KSE Oil Tracker, CREA monthly analyses, Kpler vessel data\).116 A dedicated commercial satellite verification program would cost an estimated $5 to $50 million annually, a fraction of the OSCE SMM's peak budget of over 100 million euros and orders of magnitude less than the revenue at stake.)
