/P 638 0 R
/T (OFAC's authorized staff of 261 full-time equivalents handles routine enforcement, not the sustained campaign this framework requires; the GAO's September 2025 audit found that agencies have not established measurable outcomes for sanctions activities.119 Verification costs of $5 to $50 million annually compare favorably to the OSCE SMM's 100 million euros with 1,300 staff. Market price effects from Phase I may produce a temporary Brent increase of $5 to $10 per barrel, manageable within the IEA's projected surplus and OPEC's spare capacity. Phase III relief eases prices in the medium term.)
/E (OFAC's authorized staff of 261 full-time equivalents handles routine enforcement, not the sustained campaign this framework requires; the GAO's September 2025 audit found that agencies have not established measurable outcomes for sanctions activities.119 Verification costs of $5 to $50 million annually compare favorably to the OSCE SMM's 100 million euros with 1,300 staff. Market price effects from Phase I may produce a temporary Brent increase of $5 to $10 per barrel, manageable within the IEA's projected surplus and OPEC's spare capacity. Phase III relief eases prices in the medium term.)
