/Title (Secondary sanctions on India and China, which together absorb approximately 85 percent of Russian seaborne crude, represent the largest unrealized leverage. The October 2025 designations produced measurable behavioral change: India's Russian crude intake fell 29 percent month-on-month by December, approximately 150 million barrels of Russian crude remained without buyers at sea by February 2026, and Rystad Energy projects Russia may need to cut production by 300,000 barrels per day by spring 2026.5)
