/Title (The sanctions regime that targets Russian energy revenues evolved from a single compromise instrument, the G7 $60 per barrel price cap of December 2022, into a layered, multi-actor architecture that encompasses import embargoes, maritime service prohibitions, entity designations, vessel blacklists, a dynamic price mechanism, and secondary sanctions authority. Fifteen EU sanctions packages, two major rounds of OFAC designations, and parallel UK actions constructed this architecture incrementally, each escalation a response to evasion tactics that undermined the preceding layer.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3451 0 R
/Next 3459 0 R
>>
