/Title (Subsequent EU packages followed a consistent evasion-response pattern; each round targeted circumvention methods discovered since the preceding action. Early packages \(12th, December 2023\) addressed attestation fraud; intermediate packages designated shadow fleet vessels and restricted LNG transshipment.23 Two inflection points reshaped the architecture. The 14th package \(June 2024\) imposed an LNG transshipment ban after monitors found that EU ports had re-exported approximately 20 percent of Russian LNG that reached Europe, and designated the first 27 shadow fleet vessels. The 18th package \(July 2025\) replaced the static cap with a floating formula \(85 percent of the 22-week Urals average\) after Bank of Finland analysis found European tanker involvement in Russian oil exports had risen to approximately 50 percent, a level at which the static $60 cap enabled rather than constrained Western participation.24 The floating formula eliminated the need for repeated political negotiations and produced the September 2025 cap of $47.60 and the February 2026 cap of $44.10.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
