/Title (The mechanism's effectiveness, however, faces a structural constraint from U.S.-EU divergence: the United States retained the $60 cap, which creates a bifurcated compliance environment in which a $50 transaction is compliant under U.S. rules but non-compliant under the EU's $44.10.30 The proposed full maritime services ban would resolve this through elimination of the attestation architecture; enforcement would require only verification that a vessel did not enter a Russian port. The IEA's projection of a global oil surplus in 2026 substantially mitigates the supply-disruption risk that constrained the original design.31)
