/Title (The Urals-Brent discount, the price differential between Russia's benchmark crude and the international standard, widened from a pre-invasion norm of $1-2 per barrel to $29.20 in January 2026, and pushed average Urals prices to $37.60 per barrel.34 At this level, portions of Russian production operate near full-cycle costs of $40-45 per barrel, and some fields generate minimal or zero profit after extraction, transport, and tax obligations. The academic literature identifies the EU import embargo, not the price cap directly, as the primary mechanism behind this discount.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3483 0 R
>>
endobj
3488 0 obj
