/Title (The discount trajectory reveals a critical pattern. The spread narrowed steadily as the shadow fleet matured and contracted to $4-6 by August-September 2025, the smallest gap since the invasion. The October 2025 designations reversed this trend within weeks: the discount spiked to $23-24 in November, widened to $26-27 in December, and reached $29.20 in January 2026.38 The mechanism matters for the leverage argument: if the embargo drives the structural discount and the cap contributes primarily through its enforcement architecture, then the enforcement gap, the failure to enforce service restrictions against the shadow fleet, is the key variable. Tighter enforcement amplifies the price effect without additional sanctions legislation.)
