/Title (Ship-to-ship transfers represent the shadow fleet's critical operational technique and its most geographically concentrated vulnerability. STS transfers serve four evasion functions: vessel swap to eliminate attestation requirements, crude mixture to obscure provenance, AIS shutdown to avoid detection, and fraudulent price documentation.57 CREA reported approximately 121 million euros per day in Russian oil transferred via STS in EU waters as of August 2025; this volume collapsed to approximately 5.5 million euros per day by January 2026, a decline that reflects enforcement pressure combined with geographic displacement rather than elimination of the practice.58 The pattern is consistent across hubs: enforcement at Ceuta, Greece's Laconian Gulf, and Malaysia shifted activity to the next available location rather than a reduction in total volume. Structural solutions require enforcement at chokepoints that no alternative route can bypass: the Danish Straits, the Suez Canal, and the Strait of Malacca.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
