/Title (as the ESPO premium collapsed from positive $2 per barrel to negative $6.74 The response bifurcated along institutional lines: state-owned enterprises paused seaborne purchases within 24 hours of the October designations, but independent "teapot" refineries, approximately 150 facilities concentrated in Shandong Province that collectively constitute one-third of China's refining capacity, increased purchases.75 Pipeline deliveries of approximately 900,000 bpd continued uninterrupted. Four structural factors explain China's non-responsiveness: yuan-denominated bilateral trade reduces dollar exposure; state energy security priorities override commercial compliance incentives; retaliatory capability in rare earths and supply chains creates mutual deterrence that India cannot replicate; and the teapot refineries that handle the bulk of Russian crude operate outside the formal banking channels that OFAC can most effectively target.76 Fishman frames the policy question directly: aggressive sanctions against Chinese refineries and banks remain the most powerful unused lever, but deployment intersects with broader trade, Taiwan, and technology competition in ways that Indian sanctions did not.)
