/Title (The JCPOA offers the closest precedent for staged, verification-triggered multilateral sanctions relief. Implementation Day on January 16, 2016, demonstrated that simultaneous multi-actor relief tied to independent verification is technically achievable: the IAEA verified Iran's completion of fifteen nuclear-related actions, and the EU, United States, and United Nations lifted sanctions in coordinated sequence.87 The 2018 U.S. withdrawal, however, destroyed the framework without activating its own enforcement architecture, and Iran began to exceed nuclear limits by July 2019; Moscow explicitly cites this precedent, with Lavrov calling the snapback mechanism "a trap."88 The "JCPOA chill" reinforced the lesson from the economic side: despite formal relief, few Western firms returned to Iran, as residual sanctions, banking de-risking, and snapback risk combined to limit tangible economic benefit.89)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
