/Title (The evidence argues against this approach on both strategic and precedential grounds. Relief without prior tightening signals that the current baseline, to which Russia has already substantially adapted, represents the ceiling of Western coercive capability. Fried and Donovan at the Atlantic Council warn that "Russia will pocket concessions and consider them a sign of weakness."103 The Myanmar precedent provides the strongest cautionary case: the United States rolled back three decades of sanctions between 2011 and 2016 in response to democratic opening, the 2021 military coup reversed all gains, and reimposition faced higher political costs because the sanctions infrastructure had been dismantled. Venezuela offers a more recent parallel: the Biden administration issued a general license to incentivize free elections in 2023, and Maduro exploited the economic relief and falsified results regardless.104 Relief without tightening signals that the baseline is the ceiling.)
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3575 0 R
/Prev 3580 0 R
/Next 3581 0 R
>>
endobj
