/Title (The snapback architecture must address Moscow's explicit skepticism about U.S. commitment durability; Lavrov characterized the JCPOA snapback as "a trap."114 The FDD's general license approach provides the most operationally sound mechanism: entities remain on the SDN list throughout all three phases, and relief comes exclusively through revocable licenses. Formal SDN delisting, which requires 12-18 months for re-designation, should occur only at the final stage of comprehensive settlement compliance, years into the process. Russia's UNSC veto makes Council-based snapback architecture impossible; any mechanism must therefore operate on a purely plurilateral basis among G7 and coalition partners. CAATSA-covered designations face 30-day congressional review even for relief, a deliberate institutional brake that the Envoy should treat as a credibility asset rather than a constraint.115)
