/Title (Verification requires a hybrid architecture that bypasses the OSCE consensus problem, since Russia vetoed mandate renewal in March 2022. The alternative combines commercial satellite and AIS surveillance \(Windward, Maxar/Planet/ICEYE\), the U.S.-involved monitoring mechanism under discussion at the Geneva and Abu Dhabi rounds, and open-source intelligence from established platforms \(KSE Oil Tracker, CREA monthly analyses, Kpler vessel data\).116 A dedicated commercial satellite verification program would cost an estimated $5 to $50 million annually, a fraction of the OSCE SMM's peak budget of over 100 million euros and orders of magnitude less than the revenue at stake.)
