3615 0 obj
<<
/Title (The strategy requires alignment of an intra-administration tension before it can function as coalition strategy. Witkoff, who functions as de facto chief interlocutor, reportedly pressed to lift energy sanctions; Rubio denied this "unequivocally"; Bessent controls the sanctions machinery through Treasury and demonstrated willingness to escalate through the October designations.117 Phase I tightening must register as coordinated strategy, not internal contradiction. Congressional engagement is essential: CAATSA's 30-day review period and the Peace Through Strength Act's provisions give Congress a formal role that strengthens the framework's credibility.)
/Dest [47 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3606 0 R
/Next 3620 0 R
>>
endobj
3616 0 obj
<<
/Title (OFAC's authorized staff of 261 full-time equivalents handles routine enforcement, not the sustained campaign this framework requires; the GAO's September 2025 audit found that agencies have not established measurable outcomes for sanctions activities.119 Verification costs of $5 to $50 million annually compare favorably to the OSCE SMM's 100 million euros with 1,300 staff. Market price effects from Phase I may produce a temporary Brent increase of $5 to $10 per barrel, manageable within the IEA's projected surplus and OPEC's spare capacity. Phase III relief eases prices in the medium term.)
/Dest [47 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3606 0 R
/Prev 3620 0 R
>>
endobj
