/Title (Coalition partners for Phase I are readily available. The EU and UK have independently escalated throughout 2025 and serve as natural allies for front-loaded enforcement. Nordic and Baltic states possess the strongest enforcement motivation through environmental liability exposure. Hungary remains the most consequential spoiler, with the Paks II nuclear entanglement \(10 billion euro Rosatom loan at 80 percent of costs\) as structural motivation to obstruct; Phase I's emphasis on unilateral U.S. action specifically bypasses this constraint.118 Greece and Malta oppose the proposed maritime services ban to protect their merchant fleets. Turkey occupies a potential pivot position: imports collapsed from 400,000 to 100,000 bpd after the October designations, and the STAR refinery faces a binary choice between Russian feedstock and EU export market access, an incentive structure the Envoy could exploit.)
/Dest [47 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3606 0 R
/Prev 3615 0 R
/Next 3616 0 R
>>
endobj
